{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And Resen between Nineveh.</b> He built Resen between Nineveh and Calah, and joined Nineveh and Calah together, and they were like one great city; therefore Nineveh is called 'the great city.' Another interpretation: 'Out of that land went forth Asshur' — Asshur is the name of a person, as Rashi explained. And it is found in the midrash: what did HaShem see to appoint a prophet to rebuke Nineveh more than all other lands? Rather, in the merit of Asshur, who was righteous, for he built Nineveh, as it is written <b>Out of that land went forth Asshur</b> — meaning, from that counsel Asshur went forth, for he did not agree with the generation of the Dispersion. He was righteous, but in the end it is written 'Asshur also is joined with them' — that in the end he went astray. Resh Lakish said: you might have thought that the family of Put had disappeared, until Ezekiel came and publicized it: Put and Lud and all the Arab. And the reason they are not enumerated in the Torah: if you were to count them, you would find among them more than seventy nations."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:47.992674339Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}